{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If a matter is too extraordinary.</b> Every פְּלֵאָה is a term of distinction and separation — that the matter is set apart and hidden from you." "<b>Between blood and blood.</b> Between unclean blood and clean blood (Niddah 19)." "<b>Between ruling and ruling.</b> Between a ruling of acquittal and a ruling of guilt." "<b>Between plague-mark and plague-mark.</b> Between an unclean plague-mark and a clean plague-mark." "<b>Matters of dispute.</b> That the sages of the city are divided over the matter — this one declares unclean and this one declares clean, this one holds liable and this one holds exempt." "<b>And you shall arise and go up.</b> This teaches that the Temple is higher than all other places (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:30.061786289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}